<title>SINGAPORE: Marco Polo six months net profit up.</title>
<headline>Marco Polo six months net profit up.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-11-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year ended September 30</p>
<p>1996  (in millions of S$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit			    4.98    vs     3.07</p>
<p>    Group share (cents)		 1.25    vs     0.77</p>
<p>    Turnover			     32.31    vs    36.21</p>
<p>    Dividend (cents)		    1.00    vs     1.00</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit			6.07    vs     4.91</p>
<p>    Tax				     1.10    vs     1.85</p>
<p>    Other income			  1.19    vs     0.55</p>
<p>    Interest on borrowings	    4.35    vs     4.76</p>
<p>    Depreciation			  2.62    vs     2.36</p>
<p>    Dividend pay date	 - December 18 1996</p>
<p>Last day register close - December 9  1996  </p>
<p>Note - Hotel and property company Marc Polo Developments Ltd said comparison figures are for the six months of the preceding financial period. It attributed the higher pre-profit to tight control of operating costs, lower net interest payments and write back of an overprovision of property tax for an investment property. -- Singapore newsroom (65 8703080)</p>
</text>
